# Version / sync

`VERSION` is the release date of the **shareable** skills in this repo. See [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) for what changed in each release, and the repo's **Releases** page for the matching `v<date>` tags.

## Maintainer sync (author of this repo)

Private source of truth (may contain personal paths/IDs):
- `~/.cursor/commands/eod.md` (and sibling commands)
- Optionally `~/.claude/commands/` if that copy leads

Published skills live in `skills/` with `YOUR_*` placeholders.

```bash
# See whether local Cursor commands drifted from published skills
./scripts/check-drift.sh

# Re-sanitize from local Cursor commands into skills/ (review the diff!)
./scripts/sync-from-local.sh
# then: add a CHANGELOG.md entry for the new date, bump VERSION date, commit, and
# cut a GitHub release tagged v<date> with that CHANGELOG entry as the notes:
#   gh release create "v$(cat VERSION | head -1)" -t "$(cat VERSION | head -1)" -F <changelog-entry>
```

`check-drift.sh` normalizes personal vault paths, email, and Slack IDs to placeholders before diffing, so noise is mostly real instruction changes.

> **Note (2026-08-20):** `~/.claude/commands/` is now the source of truth and the scripts' default — the author has moved off Cursor. `~/.cursor/commands/` is stale and no longer synced from; delete it or ignore it. Override with `LOCAL_COMMANDS_DIR` only if your own source lives elsewhere.

## Adopter

After `./scripts/install.sh`, your installed commands are a snapshot of this `VERSION`. Re-pull + re-run install to upgrade. Your `config.env` is not overwritten by git.
